{:edb/committed true :edb/basis-t 2881 :edb/replayed false :edb/tx-hash "0dabd0760258969bc2437721185c8374d26edb33ceb2b55c1323c0f353da1fe7" :edb/db-before-t 2880 :edb/db-after-t 2881 :edb/tx-data [[13194139536193 50 #inst "2026-10-09T19:15:07.093Z" 13194139536193 true] [17592186119569 1145 "Note that the position vector of $Q$ is $\\mathbf{q}=\\langle \\sqrt{2},0,-5 \\rangle.$ Converting the parametric equations of the line to vector form, we get\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042677/assets/4c70e51d85874e5a241a5d9b35b147500d4c306187c5e0a1d15a48a9aef07706.png)\n\nThe direction vector of the line is $\\mathbf{v}=\\langle  0 , \\sqrt{3} , -1\\rangle,$ so a normal vector to the plane is \n\n$$\n\\mathbf{n}=\\mathbf{v}=\\langle  0 , \\sqrt{3} , -1 \\rangle.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation of the plane is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(r-q)\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n-q\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n & =q\\cdot n \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨0,\\sqrt{3},-1⟩ & =⟨\\sqrt{2},0,-5⟩\\cdot ⟨0,\\sqrt{3},-1⟩ \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨0,\\sqrt{3},-1⟩ & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139536193 false] [17592186119569 1145 "Note that the position vector of $Q$ is $\\mathbf{q}=\\langle \\sqrt{2},0,-5 \\rangle.$ Converting the parametric equations of the line to vector form, we get\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14083941/assets/3c1e2e4034bcbc860f548935ca7305bc8f141c56ba14f821fd1aa6cb2b53f8d9.png)\n\nThe direction vector of the line is $\\mathbf{v}=\\langle  0 , \\sqrt{3} , -1\\rangle,$ so a normal vector to the plane is \n\n$$\n\\mathbf{n}=\\mathbf{v}=\\langle  0 , \\sqrt{3} , -1 \\rangle.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation of the plane is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(r-q)\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n-q\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n & =q\\cdot n \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨0,\\sqrt{3},-1⟩ & =⟨\\sqrt{2},0,-5⟩\\cdot ⟨0,\\sqrt{3},-1⟩ \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨0,\\sqrt{3},-1⟩ & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139536193 true] [17592186119753 1020 #edb/ref 17592186388213 13194139536193 true] [17592186119753 1020 #edb/ref 17592186388234 13194139536193 true] [17592186119754 1020 #edb/ref 17592186388220 13194139536193 true] [17592186119754 1020 #edb/ref 17592186388227 13194139536193 true] [17592186119754 1020 #edb/ref 17592186388241 13194139536193 true] [17592186120149 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139536193 true] [17592186120149 1100 "Find an equation of the plane that contains the point $P(2,-5, 3)$ and is perpendicular to the vector $n = ⟨ - 1, 2,-3⟩$." 13194139536193 false] [17592186120149 1100 "Find an equation of the plane that contains the point $P(2,-5,3)$ and is perpendicular to the vector $n=⟨-1,2,-3⟩.$" 13194139536193 true] [17592186120149 1145 "First, we note that the position vector of $P$ is $p=⟨2,-5,3⟩,$ and $n=⟨-1,2,-3⟩$ is normal to the plane.\n\nThe equation of the plane that passes through the point $P({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})$ and is perpendicular to the vector $n$ can be given as\n\n$$\n(r-p)\\cdot n=0,\n$$\n\nwhere $r$ is the position vector of any point on the plane, and $p$ is the position vector of $P.$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(r-p)\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n-p\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n & =p\\cdot n \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨-1,2,-3⟩ & =⟨2,-5,3⟩\\cdot ⟨-1,2,-3⟩ \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨-1,2,-3⟩ & =-21.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139536193 true] [17592186388213 1017 #edb/ref 17592186388214 13194139536193 true] [17592186388213 1089 "q-127632" 13194139536193 true] [17592186388213 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139536193 true] [17592186388213 1100 "Find an equation of the plane that contains the point $P(\\sqrt{5},-1,2)$ and is perpendicular to the vector $n=\\sqrt{5}i-3j+2k.$" 13194139536193 true] [17592186388213 1113 #uuid "ebf66b7c-c02a-589a-bf6a-2d48ae5c66f0" 13194139536193 true] [17592186388213 1145 "First, we note that the position vector of $P$ is $p=\\sqrt{5}i-j+2k,$ and $n=\\sqrt{5}i-3j+2k$ is normal to the plane.\n\nThe equation of the plane that passes through the point $P({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})$ and is perpendicular to the vector $n$ can be given as\n\n$$\n(r-p)\\cdot n=0,\n$$\n\nwhere $r$ is the position vector of any point on the plane, and $p$ is the position vector of $P.$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(r-p)\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n-p\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n & =p\\cdot n \\\\ r\\cdot (\\sqrt{5}i-3j+2k) & =(\\sqrt{5}i-j+2k)\\cdot (\\sqrt{5}i-3j+2k) \\\\ r\\cdot (\\sqrt{5}i-3j+2k) & =12.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139536193 true] [17592186388214 1000 #edb/ref 17592186388215 13194139536193 true] [17592186388214 1000 #edb/ref 17592186388216 13194139536193 true] [17592186388214 1000 #edb/ref 17592186388217 13194139536193 true] [17592186388214 1000 #edb/ref 17592186388218 13194139536193 true] [17592186388214 1000 #edb/ref 17592186388219 13194139536193 true] [17592186388214 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139536193 true] [17592186388214 1041 "selection" 13194139536193 true] [17592186388214 1104 #edb/ref 17592186388218 13194139536193 true] [17592186388214 1110 #uuid "7bc7438a-c90e-5587-a424-da9ae19cc227" 13194139536193 true] [17592186388215 1034 "r\\cdot (5i-3j+2k)=1" 13194139536193 true] [17592186388215 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536193 true] [17592186388215 1111 #uuid "90838ea8-74d7-56bf-9ac7-24deb39925d9" 13194139536193 true] [17592186388216 1034 "r\\cdot (\\sqrt{5}i+2j-3k)=6" 13194139536193 true] [17592186388216 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536193 true] [17592186388216 1111 #uuid "22299f7d-aef2-5792-a599-5b7cdbd54798" 13194139536193 true] [17592186388217 1034 "r\\cdot (\\sqrt{5}i-3j+2k)=6" 13194139536193 true] [17592186388217 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536193 true] [17592186388217 1111 #uuid "1b2b0286-66e8-516f-a8b7-1ca48dcba398" 13194139536193 true] [17592186388218 1034 "r\\cdot (\\sqrt{5}i-3j+2k)=12" 13194139536193 true] [17592186388218 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536193 true] [17592186388218 1111 #uuid "5578b1ed-02f4-511b-9cf9-f71ebee10f3b" 13194139536193 true] [17592186388219 1034 "r\\cdot (\\sqrt{5}i-j-2k)=12" 13194139536193 true] [17592186388219 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536193 true] [17592186388219 1111 #uuid "2afa7e37-9476-5a37-a9ae-586bd4f465d8" 13194139536193 true] [17592186388220 1017 #edb/ref 17592186388221 13194139536193 true] [17592186388220 1089 "q-127911" 13194139536193 true] [17592186388220 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139536193 true] [17592186388220 1100 "A nonzero vector $⟨a,\\,0,\\,c⟩$ is parallel to the plane $r\\cdot ⟨-1,2,2⟩=\\sqrt{11}.$ What is the value of $\\frac{a}{c}?$" 13194139536193 true] [17592186388220 1113 #uuid "2106ae49-d1a1-5883-81b7-3f9a97f85eb1" 13194139536193 true] [17592186388220 1145 "We need a vector $v=⟨{t}_{1},{t}_{2},{t}_{3}⟩$ that is parallel to the given plane. \n\nFrom the equation $r\\cdot ⟨-1,2,2⟩=\\sqrt{11}$ of the plane, we get the normal vector $n=⟨-1,2,2⟩.$ So, $v⊥n$ and we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ ⟨{t}_{1},{t}_{2},{t}_{3}⟩\\cdot ⟨-1,2,2⟩ & =0 \\\\ -{t}_{1}+2{t}_{2}+2{t}_{3} & =0 \\\\ {t}_{1} & =2{t}_{2}+2{t}_{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, we obtain \n\n$$\nv=⟨2{t}_{2}+2{t}_{3},\\,{t}_{2},\\,{t}_{3}⟩,\n$$\n\nwhere ${t}_{2},{t}_{3}\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$ \n\nWe are told that the second component of $v$ equals $0.$ So, we must set ${t}_{2}=0.$ \n\nSince $v$ is nonzero, we can pick any ${t}_{3}\\ne 0.$ For example, setting ${t}_{3}=1$, we get\n\n$$\nv=⟨2,\\,0,\\,1⟩.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\frac{a}{c}=2.$" 13194139536193 true] [17592186388221 1000 #edb/ref 17592186388222 13194139536193 true] [17592186388221 1000 #edb/ref 17592186388223 13194139536193 true] [17592186388221 1000 #edb/ref 17592186388224 13194139536193 true] [17592186388221 1000 #edb/ref 17592186388225 13194139536193 true] [17592186388221 1000 #edb/ref 17592186388226 13194139536193 true] [17592186388221 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139536193 true] [17592186388221 1041 "selection" 13194139536193 true] [17592186388221 1104 #edb/ref 17592186388224 13194139536193 true] [17592186388221 1110 #uuid "a1b427c8-4111-57d9-a559-b96d86abedcb" 13194139536193 true] [17592186388222 1034 "\\sqrt{11}" 13194139536193 true] [17592186388222 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536193 true] [17592186388222 1111 #uuid "8a9c6dcb-f573-5d83-9ff7-531ac1aeb53b" 13194139536193 true] [17592186388223 1034 "\\frac{1}{2}" 13194139536193 true] [17592186388223 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536193 true] [17592186388223 1111 #uuid "d182a9a4-c04f-5326-bf96-030c530e879d" 13194139536193 true] [17592186388224 1034 "2" 13194139536193 true] [17592186388224 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536193 true] [17592186388224 1111 #uuid "29ec928d-4fed-511e-98bf-bc72adf8d237" 13194139536193 true] [17592186388225 1034 "1" 13194139536193 true] [17592186388225 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536193 true] [17592186388225 1111 #uuid "3c2ccf46-b6bf-5c86-a235-83216f4e9d24" 13194139536193 true] [17592186388226 1034 "-2" 13194139536193 true] [17592186388226 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536193 true] [17592186388226 1111 #uuid "7b561743-8705-5b8a-8882-eca15c6a78a9" 13194139536193 true] [17592186388227 1017 #edb/ref 17592186388228 13194139536193 true] [17592186388227 1089 "q-33313" 13194139536193 true] [17592186388227 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139536193 true] [17592186388227 1100 "A nonzero vector $⟨a,\\,0,\\,c⟩$ is parallel to the plane $r\\cdot ⟨4,0,2⟩=16.$ What is the value of $\\frac{a}{c}?$" 13194139536193 true] [17592186388227 1113 #uuid "1f6dc541-437c-58b0-a5ee-063fc6840b9a" 13194139536193 true] [17592186388227 1145 "We need a vector $v=⟨{t}_{1},{t}_{2},{t}_{3}⟩$ that is parallel to the given plane. \n\nFrom the equation $r\\cdot ⟨4,0,2⟩=16$ of the plane, we get the normal vector $n=⟨4,0,2⟩.$ So, $v⊥n$ and we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ ⟨{t}_{1},{t}_{2},{t}_{3}⟩\\cdot ⟨4,0,2⟩ & =0 \\\\ 4{t}_{1}+2{t}_{3} & =0 \\\\ 2{t}_{3} & =-4{t}_{1} \\\\ {t}_{3} & =-2{t}_{1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, we obtain \n\n$$\nv=⟨{t}_{1},\\,{t}_{2},\\,-2{t}_{1}⟩,\n$$\n\nwhere ${t}_{1},{t}_{2}\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$ \n\nWe are told that the second component of $v$ equals $0.$ So, we must set ${t}_{2}=0.$ \n\nSince $v$ is nonzero, we can pick any ${t}_{1}\\ne 0.$ For example, setting ${t}_{1}=1$, we get\n\n$$\nv=⟨1,\\,0,\\,-2⟩.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\frac{a}{c}=-\\frac{1}{2}.$" 13194139536193 true] [17592186388228 1000 #edb/ref 17592186388229 13194139536193 true] [17592186388228 1000 #edb/ref 17592186388230 13194139536193 true] [17592186388228 1000 #edb/ref 17592186388231 13194139536193 true] [17592186388228 1000 #edb/ref 17592186388232 13194139536193 true] [17592186388228 1000 #edb/ref 17592186388233 13194139536193 true] [17592186388228 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139536193 true] [17592186388228 1041 "selection" 13194139536193 true] [17592186388228 1104 #edb/ref 17592186388229 13194139536193 true] [17592186388228 1110 #uuid "eca7ee86-582e-5def-9aa5-1fe4aee637d4" 13194139536193 true] [17592186388229 1034 "-\\frac{1}{2}" 13194139536193 true] [17592186388229 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536193 true] [17592186388229 1111 #uuid "3480cce1-a45e-5d9a-ae8d-ec998718688f" 13194139536193 true] [17592186388230 1034 "\\frac{1}{2}" 13194139536193 true] [17592186388230 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536193 true] [17592186388230 1111 #uuid "8390b68c-d721-5aa7-a417-f8f298695617" 13194139536193 true] [17592186388231 1034 "2" 13194139536193 true] [17592186388231 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536193 true] [17592186388231 1111 #uuid "8326e5ea-b254-5896-81e0-ba5084f3d56a" 13194139536193 true] [17592186388232 1034 "-4" 13194139536193 true] [17592186388232 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536193 true] [17592186388232 1111 #uuid "b6d88325-377d-5cce-8511-51495605e5ac" 13194139536193 true] [17592186388233 1034 "4" 13194139536193 true] [17592186388233 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536193 true] [17592186388233 1111 #uuid "385cc335-3ceb-5153-831b-8df058a3da36" 13194139536193 true] [17592186388234 1017 #edb/ref 17592186388235 13194139536193 true] [17592186388234 1089 "q-70647" 13194139536193 true] [17592186388234 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139536193 true] [17592186388234 1100 "Find an equation of the plane that passes through the point $P(1,-4,5)$ and is perpendicular to the vector $n=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 6 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].$" 13194139536193 true] [17592186388234 1113 #uuid "559832c2-15b2-5b81-bb2b-4adab3a391f2" 13194139536193 true] [17592186388234 1145 "First, notice that the position vector of $P$ is $p=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]$ and $n=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 6 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]$ is normal to the plane. \n\nThe equation of the plane that passes though the point $P({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})$ and is perpendicular to the vector $n$ can be given as\n\n$$\n(r-p)\\cdot n=0,\n$$\n\nwhere $r$ is the position vector of any point on the plane, and $p$ is the position vector of $P.$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(r-p)\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n-p\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n & =p\\cdot n \\\\ r\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 6 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 6 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\ r\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 6 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}] & =-11.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139536193 true] [17592186388235 1000 #edb/ref 17592186388236 13194139536193 true] [17592186388235 1000 #edb/ref 17592186388237 13194139536193 true] [17592186388235 1000 #edb/ref 17592186388238 13194139536193 true] [17592186388235 1000 #edb/ref 17592186388239 13194139536193 true] [17592186388235 1000 #edb/ref 17592186388240 13194139536193 true] [17592186388235 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139536193 true] [17592186388235 1041 "selection" 13194139536193 true] [17592186388235 1104 #edb/ref 17592186388240 13194139536193 true] [17592186388235 1110 #uuid "7b7484f5-85f7-5b94-b8ee-9fb636c134a6" 13194139536193 true] [17592186388236 1034 "r\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 6 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]" 13194139536193 true] [17592186388236 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536193 true] [17592186388236 1111 #uuid "364eac3b-e0ca-5f00-867e-8707462b7cc6" 13194139536193 true] [17592186388237 1034 "r\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 6 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]" 13194139536193 true] [17592186388237 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536193 true] [17592186388237 1111 #uuid "0a31383c-ff79-5565-90a9-06ed987e7c20" 13194139536193 true] [17592186388238 1034 "r\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]=9" 13194139536193 true] [17592186388238 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536193 true] [17592186388238 1111 #uuid "424550e6-88ec-5364-9608-4cb87b21b87c" 13194139536193 true] [17592186388239 1034 "r\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 6 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]=-20" 13194139536193 true] [17592186388239 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536193 true] [17592186388239 1111 #uuid "7329a3d9-cbe9-5c7d-a9d2-2c2a2bda2f90" 13194139536193 true] [17592186388240 1034 "r\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 6 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]=-11" 13194139536193 true] [17592186388240 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536193 true] [17592186388240 1111 #uuid "5a9d625c-e119-56a8-b497-b0feaf333432" 13194139536193 true] [17592186388241 1017 #edb/ref 17592186388242 13194139536193 true] [17592186388241 1089 "q-70822" 13194139536193 true] [17592186388241 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139536193 true] [17592186388241 1100 "A nonzero vector $⟨a,\\,b,\\,0⟩$ is parallel to the plane $r\\cdot ⟨-5,-1,4⟩=6.$ What is the value of $\\frac{a}{b}?$" 13194139536193 true] [17592186388241 1113 #uuid "df678eb7-55a1-58ab-b1a0-68980ffc732f" 13194139536193 true] [17592186388241 1145 "We need a vector $v=⟨{t}_{1},{t}_{2},{t}_{3}⟩$ that is parallel to the given plane. \n\nFrom the equation $r\\cdot ⟨-5,-1,4⟩=6$ of the plane, we get the normal vector $n=⟨-5,-1,4⟩.$ So, $v⊥n$ and we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ ⟨{t}_{1},{t}_{2},{t}_{3}⟩\\cdot ⟨-5,-1,4⟩ & =0 \\\\ -5{t}_{1}-{t}_{2}+4{t}_{3} & =0 \\\\ {t}_{2} & =-5{t}_{1}+4{t}_{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, we obtain \n\n$$\nv=⟨{t}_{1},-5{t}_{1}+4{t}_{3},{t}_{3}⟩,\n$$\n\nwhere ${t}_{1},{t}_{3}\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$ \n\nWe are told that the third component of $v$ equals $0.$ So, we must set ${t}_{3}=0.$ \n\nSince $v$ is nonzero, we can pick any ${t}_{1}\\ne 0.$ For example, setting ${t}_{1}=1$, we get\n\n$$\nv=⟨1,\\,-5,\\,0⟩.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\frac{a}{b}=-\\frac{1}{5}.$" 13194139536193 true] [17592186388242 1000 #edb/ref 17592186388243 13194139536193 true] [17592186388242 1000 #edb/ref 17592186388244 13194139536193 true] [17592186388242 1000 #edb/ref 17592186388245 13194139536193 true] [17592186388242 1000 #edb/ref 17592186388246 13194139536193 true] [17592186388242 1000 #edb/ref 17592186388247 13194139536193 true] [17592186388242 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139536193 true] [17592186388242 1041 "selection" 13194139536193 true] [17592186388242 1104 #edb/ref 17592186388247 13194139536193 true] [17592186388242 1110 #uuid "9e377c1a-e345-5529-a86c-041ad412386c" 13194139536193 true] [17592186388243 1034 "\\frac{1}{4}" 13194139536193 true] [17592186388243 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536193 true] [17592186388243 1111 #uuid "3d93d805-9f4d-5e11-b71e-dbdd1ffa2381" 13194139536193 true] [17592186388244 1034 "-\\frac{5}{4}" 13194139536193 true] [17592186388244 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536193 true] [17592186388244 1111 #uuid "e525008f-72fa-52f9-ab3e-24568668c21a" 13194139536193 true] [17592186388245 1034 "\\frac{1}{5}" 13194139536193 true] [17592186388245 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536193 true] [17592186388245 1111 #uuid "0d12685e-070c-5e87-80ec-f550d4b1492e" 13194139536193 true] [17592186388246 1034 "5" 13194139536193 true] [17592186388246 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536193 true] [17592186388246 1111 #uuid "4fb71b55-877c-5b65-828b-61a62605d82a" 13194139536193 true] [1759